 "commit": "96675309c86b955092040f77068217dbeb1f50f2",
 "observations": [
  "Darker brown streaks run across the crown in every view, on both backends.",
  "A dark brown patch sits at the side of the neck in the three-quarter and full-body views. It is the floppy ear, which B2 asks to be darker than the coat.",
  "From the low hero angle a thin pale line runs along the lower lip's edge, and a small white highlight sits at the front of the closed mouth, where the front teeth are.",
  "At the extreme eye and nose close-ups (a 20 degree field a few tens of centimetres away) the face and muzzle strands read as flat, hard-edged ribbons radiating from the skin. From the face close-up outward they read as fur.",
  "Stray hairs stand out of the head's outline against the sky in the face close-up.",
  "In the rear views the tail's pale tip glows white where the sun shines through it, blown out to a soft white patch (the runtime rear footage and the RearTail still, both backends).",
  "Through the dolly, from the 11 m step outward, the coat reads as clumped curls in the enlarged crops; at native size the dog is a few dozen pixels tall there. At the 22.5 m card hand-over the coat is blotchier than the strands just before it.",
  "In the panting footage the tongue lies over the lower teeth and hangs past the lip; no tooth shows through it. Its highlights are broad and soft rather than lacquered, and the lower canine shows white at the corner of the mouth.",
  "The eye's catch-light is a small steady highlight in every view on both backends, including the low hero view where a white bloom used to appear.",
  "OpenGL and Vulkan show the same pose and the same coat in all six hero views and on all three paths; the visible differences are the wind-blown grass blades in front of the camera."
 ],
